{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"timers","title":"Timers & Cancellation","group":"Asynchronous JavaScript","order":46,"html":"<p class=\"lead\"><code>setTimeout</code>, <code>setInterval</code>, <code>setImmediate</code>, <code>queueMicrotask</code> and <code>AbortController</code> — scheduling work and cancelling it.</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>API</th><th>Schedules</th><th>Cancel with</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>setTimeout(fn, ms, ...args)</code></td><td>Once, after at least <code>ms</code></td><td><code>clearTimeout(id)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>setInterval(fn, ms)</code></td><td>Repeatedly every <code>ms</code></td><td><code>clearInterval(id)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>setImmediate(fn)</code> (Node)</td><td>Once, in the check phase</td><td><code>clearImmediate(id)</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>queueMicrotask(fn)</code></td><td>As a microtask</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td><code>requestAnimationFrame(fn)</code> (browser)</td><td>Before the next repaint</td><td><code>cancelAnimationFrame(id)</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const id = setTimeout(() =&gt; console.log(\"never printed\"), 10);\nclearTimeout(id);\n\nsetTimeout((a, b) =&gt; console.log(\"args:\", a, b), 5, \"x\", \"y\");\n\nlet n = 0;\nconst iv = setInterval(() =&gt; {\n  n++;\n  console.log(\"tick\", n);\n  if (n === 3) clearInterval(iv);\n}, 5);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>args: x y\ntick 1\ntick 2\ntick 3</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-hourglass\"></i>Delays are minimums</h3>\n<ul><li>The callback runs <strong>at least</strong> <code>ms</code> later — later if the stack is busy.</li><li>Browsers clamp nested timers (5+ levels deep) to ≥ 4 ms and throttle background tabs to ≥ 1 s.</li><li><code>setInterval</code> does not wait for slow callbacks; prefer a recursive <code>setTimeout</code> when each run must finish before the next is scheduled.</li></ul>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const start = performance.now();\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; {\n  console.log(\"waited at least 20ms:\", performance.now() - start &gt;= 20);\n}, 10);\nwhile (performance.now() - start &lt; 20) {}   // block the thread for 20ms</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>waited at least 20ms: true</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-clock-play\"></i>Promise-based timers</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>import { setTimeout as sleep } from \"node:timers/promises\";\nconst sleepAnywhere = (ms) =&gt; new Promise((r) =&gt; setTimeout(r, ms));   // browser version\n\nconsole.log(await sleep(5, \"node timers/promises\"));\nawait sleepAnywhere(5);\nconsole.log(\"slept\");</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>node timers/promises\nslept</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-hand-stop\"></i>Cancellation with AbortController</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function cancellableDelay(ms, { signal } = {}) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) =&gt; {\n    if (signal?.aborted) return reject(signal.reason);\n    const id = setTimeout(resolve, ms, \"finished\");\n    signal?.addEventListener(\"abort\", () =&gt; {\n      clearTimeout(id);\n      reject(signal.reason);\n    }, { once: true });\n  });\n}\nconst controller = new AbortController();\nsetTimeout(() =&gt; controller.abort(new Error(\"user cancelled\")), 10);\ntry {\n  await cancellableDelay(1000, { signal: controller.signal });\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.message);\n}\ntry {\n  await cancellableDelay(1000, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10) });\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.name);\n}</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>user cancelled\nTimeoutError</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>fetch(url, { signal })</code>, <code>addEventListener(…, { signal })</code>, Node streams and <code>timers/promises</code> all accept an <code>AbortSignal</code> — one controller can cancel a whole group of operations.</p></div>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why might setTimeout(fn, 0) not run immediately?</summary><div><p>It only queues a macrotask. It runs after the current synchronous code, after all microtasks, and after any earlier timers — and browsers may clamp the delay.</p></div></details></section>"}